	| Description | This is the partner role |
	| Name        | Partner                  |
	| Type        | Account                  |
	And I assign the team with the name "Koroneiki Partner" on the account "Korpro - ${staticCompanyName}" to the following roles
	| Partner |
	And I log into the provisioning homepage as "test@liferay.com" with password "kwSgiajslgb7ecsD"
	And I go to the product index page
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | A Liferay Portal Product |
	| Type | Select | Primary                  |
	And I click on the new product button
	And I populate and save the product form with the following values
	| Name | Input  | Gold Subscription |
	| Type | Select | Add On            |
	And I search the products page using the keyword "A"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name | A Liferay Portal Product |
	When I search the products page using the keyword "Gold"
	Then I should be able to view a product on the provisioning index with the name "Gold Subscription" and the following values
	| Name | Gold Subscription |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "A Liferay Portal Product" and the following values
	| Name                    | A Liferay Portal Product |         |
	| Product Field and Value | type                     | primary |
	And I should be able to view a koroneiki product with the name "Gold Subscription" and the following values
	| Name                    | Gold Subscription |        |
	| Product Field and Value | type              | add-on |

Scenario: Create products with duplicate names
	Testing the ability to attempt to create products with names that already exist in the provisioning product index 

	Given I generate several static variables for Provisioning
	And I generate a provisioning company name
	And I generate a provisioning project name
